{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.RothGammaProducer","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mathlib.RothGammaProducer","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.RothRealLadder"],"declarations":20,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.roth_three","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.roth_three","kind":"theorem","line":258,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RothGammaProducer.lean#L258-L269","doc":"**Roth's Lemma at `m = 3`, `t = 1/2`, on a produced `Γ_3`.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.gamma_three","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.gamma_three","kind":"theorem","line":224,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RothGammaProducer.lean#L224-L240","doc":"**`Γ_3` produced from height data, at `t = 1/2 < 1`.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.hw_large","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.hw_large","kind":"theorem","line":214,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RothGammaProducer.lean#L214-L222","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.hw_grow","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.hw_grow","kind":"theorem","line":208,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RothGammaProducer.lean#L208-L212","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.deg2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.deg2","kind":"theorem","line":203,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RothGammaProducer.lean#L203-L206","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.deg1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.deg1","kind":"theorem","line":198,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RothGammaProducer.lean#L198-L201","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.deg0","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.deg0","kind":"theorem","line":193,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RothGammaProducer.lean#L193-L196","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.hw_two_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.hw_two_le","kind":"theorem","line":189,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RothGammaProducer.lean#L189-L191","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.Nw","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.Nw","kind":"def","line":187,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RothGammaProducer.lean#L187-L187","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.Hw","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.Hw","kind":"def","line":186,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RothGammaProducer.lean#L186-L186","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.rothGammaFull_of_heights","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.rothGammaFull_of_heights","kind":"theorem","line":134,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RothGammaProducer.lean#L134-L164","doc":"**`Γ_m`, produced.**  Given heights that grow rapidly enough and a common scale `N`, the\nnormalised degrees satisfy every clause of `RothGammaFull`.\n\n⚠ This is the first construction of `Γ_m` in the arc that is not a transport\n(`rename_equiv`), a descent (`rothGammaFull_descend`), or a hand-built literal.  Clauses 1 and 2\ncome from the normalisation; 3a, 3b and 4 are conditions on `F` and `b` that the caller supplies,\nbecause they constrain data this construction does not choose. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.rothDegrees_growth","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.rothDegrees_growth","kind":"theorem","line":120,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RothGammaProducer.lean#L120-L132","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.rothDegrees_growth_nat","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.rothDegrees_growth_nat","kind":"theorem","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RothGammaProducer.lean#L94-L118","doc":"**Clause 1 holds once the degrees are large enough**, and `p·d_j ≥ p + 2q` is exactly how\nlarge.  That is Roth's \"choose `r₁` sufficiently large\", made a finite arithmetic condition. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.rothDegrees_height","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.rothDegrees_height","kind":"theorem","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RothGammaProducer.lean#L84-L92","doc":"**Clause 2 holds on the nose.**  The floor at index `0` and the ceiling elsewhere put\n`H₀^{d₀} ≤ N < H_k^{d_k}`, which is exactly \"the first `K^s` is the smallest\". ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.rothDegrees_sub_one_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.rothDegrees_sub_one_le","kind":"theorem","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RothGammaProducer.lean#L80-L82","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.lt_rothDegrees","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.lt_rothDegrees","kind":"theorem","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RothGammaProducer.lean#L76-L78","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.lt_rothDegrees_succ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.lt_rothDegrees_succ","kind":"theorem","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RothGammaProducer.lean#L72-L74","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.rothDegrees_zero_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.rothDegrees_zero_le","kind":"theorem","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RothGammaProducer.lean#L68-L70","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.rothDegrees","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.rothDegrees","kind":"def","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RothGammaProducer.lean#L60-L66","doc":"**The degree vector Roth's setup produces from a height vector.**\n\nEvery `H h ^ d h` is pinned to the same scale `N` — Mahler's normalisation `r_h·log H_h ≈ const`,\nwritten without logarithms.  The first index takes the **floor** and the rest the **ceiling**,\nwhich is what makes clause 2 (`H₁^{r₁}` smallest) hold on the nose rather than up to rounding. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.two_mul_lt_of_height_growth","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.two_mul_lt_of_height_growth","kind":"theorem","line":40,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RothGammaProducer.lean#L40-L58","doc":"**The producer's core.**  Rapid height growth turns a pair of `Nat.log` brackets into an\ninteger inequality between the degrees.  No logarithm appears in the statement, and none in the\nproof — `Γ_m`'s clauses are multiplicative, so the whole normalisation is `Nat.pow` monotonicity. ","signatureChunk":0}]}